<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd"
  identifier="stats-02" title="Muffins and the standard deviation" adaptive="false" time-dependent="false" xml:lang="en">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-correct-response>
      <qti-value>1.99</qti-value>
    </qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value>
      <qti-value>0</qti-value>
    </qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="MAXSCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float">
    <qti-default-value>
      <qti-value>1</qti-value>
    </qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-stylesheet href="stats.css" type="text/css"/>
  <qti-item-body>
    <p>A campus café counted how many chocolate muffins it sold each day for one week.</p>
    <p class="qti-align-center">
      <img src="images/muffins.svg" width="520" height="262" alt="Bar chart of chocolate muffins sold per day for one week: Monday 6, Tuesday 4, Wednesday 5, Thursday 7, Friday 6, Saturday 8, Sunday 10. A dashed line marks the mean of about 6.57."/>
    </p>
    <div class="stats-formula">
      <p>The sample standard deviation is</p>
      <p class="qti-align-center"><math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" display="block"><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><munderover><mo>&#x2211;</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>&#x2212;</mo><mover><mi>x</mi><mo>&#x203E;</mo></mover><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>&#x2212;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math></p>
    </div>
    <p>Treat the seven days as a sample. What is the standard deviation of the number of muffins sold per day? Round to two decimals and use a decimal point.</p>
    <p><em>s</em> = <qti-text-entry-interaction class="qti-input-width-6" response-identifier="RESPONSE" expected-length="6" placeholder-text="0.00"/></p>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
    <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE">
      <qti-base-value base-type="float">0</qti-base-value>
    </qti-set-outcome-value>
    <qti-response-condition>
      <qti-response-if>
        <qti-equal-rounded rounding-mode="decimalPlaces" figures="2">
          <qti-variable identifier="RESPONSE"/>
          <qti-correct identifier="RESPONSE"/>
        </qti-equal-rounded>
        <qti-set-outcome-value identifier="SCORE">
          <qti-sum>
            <qti-variable identifier="SCORE"/>
            <qti-base-value base-type="float">1</qti-base-value>
          </qti-sum>
        </qti-set-outcome-value>
      </qti-response-if>
    </qti-response-condition>
  </qti-response-processing>
</qti-assessment-item>
